xwayland: add xwayland:scale, one scale for X11 windows on every monitor

One X server serves every monitor, and an X11 app draws at one scale. With
force_zero_scaling, X11 coordinates are each monitor's pixels, so an app
drawn for a 2x panel is twice its size on a 1x monitor beside it; without
it, X11 windows are 1x and enlarged, blurry, on the 2x panel.

xwayland:scale (a float, 0 by default, which keeps today's behaviour) puts X11
coordinates at that scale on every monitor: a monitor is told to XWayland at
its logical size times the scale (its pixels when the scale is its own), X11
windows keep their logical size wherever they are, and they are drawn 1:1 on
a monitor of that scale and scaled to its size on the others, without
nearest-neighbour filtering where they are shrunk. Changing the option, or
force_zero_scaling, at runtime rearranges XWayland's outputs and reconfigures
the X11 windows.

Also: with force_zero_scaling, the monitor a Wayland coordinate is on was
found by comparing the logical coordinate with the monitor's pixel size.

For Nova: packaging/hyprland/PKGBUILD applies this to Hyprland 0.57.2's
release tarball (patch -Np1); packaging/hyprland/UPSTREAM.md is the pull
request it is offered as. Made against the tag v0.57.2.

